  "description": "OFEJER crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C130 H80 Eu4 Li2 N10 O22,3(C4 H10 O2). From the CIF bond table, Eu1A (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu2A (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu1B (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu2B (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu7 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors; Eu8 (Eu) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.486-3.793 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.91-120.57°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C142H110Eu4Li2N10O28.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
